{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1536805-homebrew-oath-of-loyalty-a-coterie-connecting-oath","id":1536805,"title":"[Homebrew] Oath of Loyalty - A Coterie connecting Oath","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-04T10:11:02-07:00","id":1536805,"title":"[Homebrew] Oath of Loyalty - A Coterie connecting Oath","content":"Hello there, I'm preparing for a new game and as part of the preparation have written up this merit, which I intend to gift to the players, as part of their introduction to the City. Feedback and thoughts are welcome: <hr /> <b><b>Oath of Loyalty (\u2022</b></b><b><b>\u2022</b></b>\u200b<b><b>\u2022) (Edited, to add another dot, originally the merit was posted as 2 dots) </b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> Effect: Your character has sworn loyalty to her coterie, and jointly as a coterie sworn loyalty to the Liege. Each vassal within the coterie buys this merit, although some campaigns can choose to grant this merit for free.<br /> <br /> Kindred often share their vitae, mixing it together as part of swearing of this oath. Vassals drinking this mixture form a Level one Blood Bond to all members of the coterie and the Liege which does not naturally resolve for as long as this Oath is in effect, even if a level 3 blood bond is formed. After the swearing of this Oath, any other Blood Bonds shatter, and any Vitae Addiction Conditions resolve.<br /> <br /> The Coterie\u2019s bond is now reinforced by the Blood, and enables them to share resources, reputations and even some of their abilities.<br /> <br /> The Coterie gains a pool of Coterie beats and XP. Whether a member of the coterie earns a point of XP add a beat to the Coterie. Just like for characters 5 beats convert to 1 XP.<br /> <br /> Coterie XP can be spent to buy merits, which could logically be shared by the Coterie, such as Allies, Resources, Safe Place, Haven, etc. The coterie merits are accessible by anyone within the coterie, and otherwise follow limitations normally.<br /> <br /> In addition to this, once per Chapter, a character within the Coterie may use a merit or a devotion of another character within the Coterie. This applies to all merits, including fighting styles and the like. The character must meet all prerequisites of the said merit.<br /> <br /> The Liege of this Oath may set an Aspiration for the Coterie. This functions as a 4th Aspiration for members of the Coterie, and grants 1 Beat to each member of the Coterie and another Beat to the Coterie pool once fulfilled. The aspiration is intuitive and the coterie need not meet or hear from the Liege in order to sense the shift in priorities.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Any social faux, breach of the law, negative rumors and the like affect everyone within the coterie. If a character within the coterie would suffer a social penalty when interacting with Kindred, other characters within the coterie also suffer that penalty reduced by 1. \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 06-04-2024, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T13:52:04-07:00","id":1536809,"title":"","content":"Coterie experience is both too much for a two-dot Merit and doesn't really add to the flavor of the oath, I think. I'm not telling you not to use it, but simply saying that rather than have that as part of this Merit, just say that in the house rules for this game this is a benefit coteries get.<br /> <br /> Is this intended to provide immunity to blood bonds and vitae addiction, or simply to break any that's preexisting at the moment the oath is sworn? The former, again, I think too much.<br /> <br /> I like the shared use of Merits and Devotions and the coterie aspiration. Those are neat and feel apt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T15:26:09-07:00","id":1536811,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a>, but I also think you should take a look at some similar rules to see what you think of them and how they relate to your merit.<br /> <br /> There are many similarities between your merit and the Colony rules on Guide to the Night. Also with the Vaulderie, a ritual from VtM. Finally, there's also a resemblance with some of the group rules in the Contagion Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Other than that, if you don't want to read any of those (or has already and still want the merit as is), I'd only remove the group Beats and make them a chronicle rule, not a merit benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T18:08:06-07:00","id":1536824,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the responses!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> <br /> On the cost: You're right, I've looked more at other Oaths and this is pretty low. 3 feels more appropriate now. However, that's only with keeping the Coterie XP benefit. The shared use of Merit/Devotion, as it's limited to once per chapter, and everyone in the coterie needs to buy this oath is more like 1 Dot merit. Note the once per chapter limitation is meant to be Coterie wide, meaning that if a coterie mate uses that benefit in a chapter, you don't get to. <br /> <br /> As for the flavor of the Oath - sort of disagree there. Why would co-owning merits not fit an oath meant to forge stronger loyalty between the group? <br /> <br /> I'll adjust the dot value of the merit to 3. I'm keeping the XP in <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> On Blood Bond/Addiction: defo no immunity, it's just meant to break the ones existing, and the addiction part is specifically added so that the whole coterie doesn't end up with multiple Vitae Addictions from swearing of this Oath itself.<br /> <br /> However, the implications of being able to break things from the past - feel quite neat to me. &quot;Sure Invictus can fix your addiction problem - you'll just need to work with these Kindred under this Liege&quot; <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <br /> <br /> Thanks, I checked out The Colony, that seemed a bit more extreme, and <i>permanent</i> than what I'd like to include. I feel like both can coexist! I do not have access to contagion chronicles and don't intend to get that, so can't compare to the rules there. <br /> <br /> As for group XP - thanks for calling it out and letting me rethink. I think it should be tied with the merit, after all, the said XP likely will be spent on specific Allies/Contacts in the Kindred world - who will have higher trust in the group because they made this Oath! Having the Oath reinforce and support their trustworthiness can be one of the reasons why Kindred are happy to ally up to the group, as opposed to individuals within it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T20:42:39-07:00","id":1536831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1536805-homebrew-oath-of-loyalty-a-coterie-connecting-oath?p=1536824#post1536824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the flavor of the Oath - sort of disagree there. Why would co-owning merits not fit an oath meant to forge stronger loyalty between the group?</div> </div> </div> </div>Co-owning Merits is fine! I don't think you <i>need</i> an oath to co-own social Merits. (In fact I think at least some books explicitly shout out sharing Safe Place in this manner.) What feels off for me is <i>creating extra experience for developing more shared Merits than you would otherwise have.</i> Being part of a coterie that has this Oath is conjuring more character resources that coteries without this Oath hypothetically wouldn't get. Being part of the sworn coterie is, by creating extra beats, creating wealth. This is why I suggest keeping the extra coterie beats, but as a house rule attached to the concept of coteries rather than as part of the writing of the Merit: this isn't a <i>power,</i> this is just a game design conceit to encourage and enable the players to develop shared infrastructure more easily.<br /> <br /> (Messing with beat income is also just generally tricky game design terrain to work with in powers that you buy with beats. You don't really want to make character advancement into an investment game of figuring out what to buy now so your portfolio will grow to afford more later. Turning it into just a rule of how player characters work in this game avoids making this into a Merit that you spend points on to get points back.)<br /> <br /> It's honestly a nitpick, since the outcome in play will be the same. It's not like you're tracking NPC coteries' beat gain and character advancement. But it's best practices in identifying what goes in a Merit and makes this something you can more freely share for use in other games without having to specify that it's tweaked for a particular purpose that might not match how another game runs.<br /> <br /> Conversely, actually, I would encourage you to allow <i>each</i> character who has sworn this Oath to separately be able to borrow a Merit or Devotion through the Oath power per session. Once per session keeps it as something that you're not drawing too freely on (but if it feels too frequent, add a Willpower cost). But you don't want only one player each session to get to take their turn having fun with the ball, and that feeling of cooperation and shared resources is stronger when they're more regularly shared.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1536805-homebrew-oath-of-loyalty-a-coterie-connecting-oath?p=1536824#post1536824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Blood Bond/Addiction: defo no immunity, it's just meant to break the ones existing, and the addiction part is specifically added so that the whole coterie doesn't end up with multiple Vitae Addictions from swearing of this Oath itself.<br /> <br /> However, the implications of being able to break things from the past - feel quite neat to me. &quot;Sure Invictus can fix your addiction problem - you'll just need to work with these Kindred under this Liege&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. This is a nice little bit of flavor that isn't overpowered, swearing this oath is not a convenient way to shrug off bonds, but it is an appropriate and potentially relevant thing to have happen when a coterie does swear this oath with each other for the first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 06-04-2024, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T02:38:47-07:00","id":1536835,"title":"","content":"While I see your point, however, there's already precedent in the game for some merits being able to &quot;increase&quot; the Beat gain rate of your coterie. Anointed is an example, although it doesn't improve your own Beat rate gain, it comes with other benefits and is a 2 dot merit. This merit - the entire group has to invest 3 XP each, and while it will pay back for itself after you've gained 15 XP (and with afaik, recommended beat gain rate of ~4-6 beats/session) that means _MONTHS_ of gametime and even then you've still got other things tied).<br /> <br /> Also, increasing &quot;wealth&quot;, for an Invictus Oath as a problem :P ? Let's not forget that first ed Invictus advantage was literally cost break for merit purchases, thus increasing &quot;wealth&quot;. This extra wealth must also be spent on shareable merits - so no acceleration in &quot;vampiric&quot; power by buying Disciplines or the like.<br /> <br /> I see your point for messing with beat gain, and the threat of there being a minigame of &quot;buying up&quot; extra beat generation as the optimal play being a problem. However, I don't think it's realistic in the current environment- especially because this merit applies to a whole coterie. If an individual was able to buy multiple beat generators, I'd be with you.<br /> <br /> I've got a solution tho! I'll make this merit 2 or 3 dots, 2 dots gives all advantages except the shared XP, 3 dots gives that in. Anyone else could then borrow the merit as is, just not allow the 3 dot version. Making it multi-dot thing, now is tempting me to add a higher tier, for also being able to borrow a discipline activation. Will refrain from this tho<br /> <br /> You've convinced me about the borrowing of merit/devotions tho. <hr /><b><b>Oath of Loyalty (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022</b></b><b><b>\u2022) </b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> Effect: Your character has sworn loyalty to her coterie, and jointly as a coterie sworn loyalty to the Liege. Each vassal within the coterie buys this merit, although some campaigns can choose to grant this merit for free.<br /> <br /> Kindred often share their vitae, mixing it together as part of swearing of this oath. Vassals drinking this mixture form a Level one Blood Bond to all members of the coterie and the Liege which does not naturally resolve for as long as this Oath is in effect, even if a level 3 blood bond is formed. After the swearing of this Oath, any other Blood Bonds shatter, and any Vitae Addiction Conditions resolve.<br /> <br /> The Coterie\u2019s bond is now reinforced by the Blood, and enables them to share resources, reputations and even some of their abilities.<br /> <br /> Once per Chapter, each character within the Coterie may use a merit or a devotion of another character within the Coterie. This applies to all merits, including fighting styles and the like. The character must meet all prerequisites of the said merit.<br /> <br /> The Liege of this Oath may set an Aspiration for the Coterie. This functions as a 4th Aspiration for members of the Coterie, and grants 1 Beat to each member of the Coterie and another Beat to the Coterie pool once fulfilled. The aspiration is intuitive and the coterie need not meet or hear from the Liege in order to sense the shift in priorities.<br /> <br /> With the 3 dot version, The Coterie gains a pool of Coterie beats and XP. Whether a member of the coterie earns a point of XP add a beat to the Coterie. Just like for characters 5 beats convert to 1 XP.<br /> <br /> Coterie XP can be spent to buy merits, which could logically be shared by the Coterie, such as Allies, Resources, Safe Place, Haven, etc. The coterie merits are accessible by anyone within the coterie, and otherwise follow limitations normally.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Any social faux, breach of the law, negative rumors and the like affect everyone within the coterie. If a character within the coterie would suffer a social penalty when interacting with Kindred, other characters within the coterie also suffer that penalty reduced by 1. \u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T13:45:28-07:00","id":1536843,"title":"","content":"The additional Coterie Beats aren't just bad Merit design, it is completely unnecessary. You're thinking about your own game and completely ignoring that a Merit you posted will be used by other people, on other tables, with other needs and contexts.<br /> <br /> Not a huge problem, since it is just a homebrew, but still a big no-no for me.<br /> <br /> What happens in a Coterie of 2? What happens in a table where not everyone get this Merit? What happens in a game with two sessions a week for three years? Those are all things that happen, even if they don't happen for you.<br /> <br /> Bad design is bad design. Since you're unmoved in this regard, then I prefer to make it clear for any other reader that I don't think this is a good idea with the shared XP rule in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T14:22:55-07:00","id":1536846,"title":"","content":"What happens in a Coterie of 2? - This should function fine for two<br /> What happens in a table where not everyone get this Merit? - They're not a coterie then are they? But yeah, this should not be available in games where not all PCs are part of the same coterie. Would it help you if I added that as a meta restriction defined in merit?<br /> What happens in a game with two sessions a week for three years? - Nothing much? If 20% extra beats with limitations on what they can be spent on breaks your table with that much XP in it, then your table was gonna break anyway.<br /> <br /> Anyway, fair enough. I personally think it is a good idea, hence being unmoved by it. I think you're overestimating how big of a thing this will be. I'm happy to loop around here with actual table experience of using this, but realistically, this just means that players won't have to crunch their heads on whether they really wanna spend 1 XP on that Contact/Allly they just met, as that puts them further away from the Discipline/Skill/Attribute they want, and who in the Coterie, if anyone should do it.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that part of this effect will turn out to be pretty small beans as far as game play goes. It looks big, because it messes with XP systems and that unnerves a lot of people, but realistically, this won't have as huge an impact as you think it will.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Did some math, so yeah, 2 sessions/week/ for 3 years, will normally end you up with somewhere in the range of 300+ XP, that's elder territory either way. Adding in an extra 60 XP which can only be spent on shared merits, is not going to cause some huge breackage to any systems or game things. This game is already running at a huge power level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 06-05-2024, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T09:24:11-07:00","id":1536872,"title":"","content":"You missed my point, so I'll try another approach.<br /> <br /> A Merit is only a Merit if taking it is optional, really optional, as in choosing to spend your points somewhere else isn't a decidedly worse option.<br /> <br /> In every single way you present this, it is a rule, not a Merit. You basically say it yourself that you don't see much sense in having this option unless everyone buys into it.<br /> <br /> Maybe the players don't all get this Merit because some of them want to spend their XP on something else. Maybe they really aren't all a Coterie, or not the same Coterie, anyways.<br /> <br /> But you dismiss the possibility precisely because you envision everyone getting it together, or not at all.<br /> <br /> This is a rule, not an option. It works fine, it just doesn't work as a Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T14:44:09-07:00","id":1536877,"title":"","content":"Point well made. You're right. And to that, here's, perhaps, the final version of the merit for the public:<br /> <br /> <b><b>Oath of Loyalty (\u2022\u2022</b></b><b><b>)</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> Effect: Your character has sworn loyalty to her coterie, and jointly as a coterie sworn loyalty to the Liege.<br /> <br /> Kindred often share their vitae, mixing it together as part of swearing of this oath. Vassals drinking this mixture form a Level one Blood Bond to all members of the coterie and the Liege which does not naturally resolve for as long as this Oath is in effect, even if a level 3 blood bond is formed. After the swearing of this Oath, any other Blood Bonds shatter, and any Vitae Addiction Conditions resolve.<br /> <br /> The Blood now reinforces the Coterie\u2019s bond, enabling them to share resources, reputations, and even some of their abilities.<br /> <br /> Once per Chapter, each character within the Coterie may use a merit or a devotion of another character within the Coterie. This applies to all merits, including fighting styles and the like. The character must meet all prerequisites of the said merit.<br /> <br /> The Liege of this Oath may set an Aspiration for the Coterie. This functions as a 4th Aspiration for members of the Coterie. The aspiration is intuitive and the coterie need not meet or hear from the Liege in order to sense the shift in priorities.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Any social faux, breach of the law, negative rumors and the like affect everyone within the coterie. If a character within the coterie would suffer a social penalty when interacting with Kindred, other characters within the coterie also suffer that penalty reduced by 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 06-06-2024, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T02:01:02-07:00","id":1537137,"title":"","content":"I think you would be better off making general Coterie rules, maybe set obligations that if met grant additional assets in the form of merits.<br /> Also I don\u2019t accept that you can categorically state that a group isn\u2019t a Coterie just because some of them don\u2019t have the same merit. Consider that a character who doesn\u2019t want to commit to serving a particular Liege is an interesting dilemma for the group to work out, a player who doesn\u2019t want to spend 3 of their hard earned XP on another player\u2019s build is a ooc problem for the table. <br /> Also the rules for sharing merits needs clarification, if a player uses another players Resources does that count as the owning players use of the merit? If not why not acquire a purchase of an availability one higher than their dots in Resources because you don\u2019t actually lose anything that way? What happens when a merit has a drawback? Can I borrow Claws of the Unholy Therefore bypassing it\u2019s drawback? Enticing, Cutthroat and Atrocious also come to mind. How do you justify True Friend or Striking Looks? Can I get a beat from Professional Training or does that occur outside of the Chapter? Can I borrow Taste if I don\u2019t have the same Speciality as the player who has it?<br /> There are too many things that need clarification and new merits could be added to the game at any time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T03:41:29-07:00","id":1537143,"title":"","content":"The group would have to resolve that conflict whether this merit is on the table or not. When most people in the group want to commit to a specific faction/powerful NPC and someone doesn't, what does your group do? How long can the 'outsider' character remain with the group? Why are they not parting ways and finding a group more aligned with their future plans? In universe - that's what would happen.<br /> Obviously, in a game, given the &quot;special&quot; status of that character as a PC, more considerations need to happen. But, I would potentially suggest that the dissenting character would transition out of PC into NPC (perhaps becoming a free ally/contact for the coterie!), or perhaps the group do not commit to serving this particular Liege at the time, prioritising the group they have, over having this commitment. Ultimately, this is a table conversation.<br /> <br /> The vast majority of tables have ST who can make a lot of these judgement calls, as they do during their role.<br /> <br /> Thank you for raising the question! The merit specifically says &quot;use their merit&quot; - you don't get a copy of that merit, you don't get to ignore the drawbacks of that merit, you don't get to choose new targets for the merit, you must meet all the prerequisites.<br /> To list the merits you mentioned:<br /> Resources: You used up your coterie friends Resources. Think of the scene from The Gentleman - where Freddy takes Eddie's cash to gamble away. The cash is gone.<br /> Claws of the Unholy: The drawback applies, so you'll need to be in Frenzy for the merit to function.<br /> Enticing, Cutthroat, Atrocious: Yup, take that 8 again for that roll if you wish, assuming you meet the prerequisites of not having the other merits.<br /> True Friend: Yup, you can go to your coterie mates True Friend and recover the WP, or you can use the Oath to apply the -5 penalty for someone to convince that ally to act against you.<br /> Taste: The Oath says you must meet the prerequisites of the merit, so obviously, you have to have the same Speciality.<br /> <br /> I think a clarification of &quot;Merit is used as is defined, meaning that any associations with other traits, or parts of the world remain the same&quot;. Not sure how to clarify this wording - tho, not even sure if this even need to be added to the actual merit, as it's clearly wording there for the rules lawyers, to which the ST can give their own answers.<br /> <br /> Overall, I don't think there's too many things to clarify. the same logic of applies to all of this - drawbacks applied, prerequisites must be met, etc. Why did you even get the idea that this would allow you to skip on drawbacks, which are parts of the merits? There is no wording to support such an interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 06-10-2024, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T09:34:17-07:00","id":1537496,"title":"","content":"I feel there\u2019s a difference between a character who doesn\u2019t have the same goals as the rest of the group and a player who doesn\u2019t want to spend XP to support another player\u2019s build. It might be best to include something that stops players from using another player\u2019s once a chapter abilities without permission to prevent bad feelings from developing but other than that it seems to do what you want it to do and everything else below is mostly just bookkeeping.<br /> I don\u2019t see any clarification on using Professional Training to get Beats when you buy new dots in a skill or an explanation for if I can use someone else\u2019s Striking Looks to get a bonus on my own rolls but I assume you will say yes.<br /> For the sake of clarity my concern with Claws and the Lashing Out merits was that having them passively produces the drawback, the drawback to Claws of the Unholy is you must use it but this merit lets you opt in to having the merit avoiding the drawback (admittedly this would require multiple members of the group to have 4 dots in the same discipline so it\u2019s not that likely to be exploited), similarly Enticing, Cutthroat and Atrocious weaken the other forms of lashing out but again you don\u2019t have the merit unless you\u2019re using it. Honestly these are not that bad but it\u2019s possible that someone will find a merit where that would become an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T03:42:09-07:00","id":1537552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel there\u2019s a difference between a character who doesn\u2019t have the same goals as the rest of the group and a player who doesn\u2019t want to spend XP to support another player\u2019s build. It might be best to include something that stops players from using another player\u2019s once a chapter abilities without permission to prevent bad feelings from developing but other than that it seems to do what you want it to do and everything else below is mostly just bookkeeping. </div> </div> </div>That sounds like table/OOC problems. A bad player, who does shit which will create bad feelings with other players, will do so regardless of this existing. A good player (or a ST running the game) will have tools to resolve that, and I would expect groups to be able to resolve these issues regardless. At least, I would fully expect my group to use those abilities of each other, with some level of consent, even if it is &quot;oh my character will be annoyed at yours, but I the player is good with this drama, so let's go&quot;. Adding in extra wording to solve these issues, feels like a plaster for a heavily bleeding wound. I might be able to prevent bad feelings from developing from <i>this</i> merit, but a player who disregards the feelings of people playing with them at the table - will disregard them elsewhere. And adding in extra clauses for these, <i>bad</i> actors does not seem like the way to actually solve the problem.<br /> <br /> Now onto the bookkeeping:<br /> At least in my games, spending of XP is out of chapter activity, and so the regular wording suffices. Obviously, that's not gonna be true, if your table allows XP spending <i>during </i>the session, especially for <i>skills dots. </i>How many tables allow XP spending during chapters? If they do, and the ST/GM takes on the extra difficulty of handling that during session, they can decide how they feel about this usage too.<br /> <br /> Yes, Striking Looks feel a bit weirder, but the IC justification for that could easily be &quot;They're friends with that hottie, I defo wanna be liked by them too&quot;, or some such.<br /> Claws of the Unholy - If you're creating a build/Coterie around being fuckin terrifying because they're a group of gangrels who will fuck you up, then that &quot;drawback&quot; isn't that much of a drawback anyway, it's a 1dot merit for a reason. If someone wants to have this, and instead of that have &quot;once per chapter, you may, while in frenzy, do an aggravated attack with your Protean 4 claws&quot;, then whatever. Let them. They're already running with someone who, if they unvolunterly frenzy will butter up whoever in their way.<br /> <br /> AND with this, they're either gambling on involuntarily falling into frenzy with targets they want to end, OR they got to Ride the Wave, which is whole bunch of extra costs and things.<br /> <br /> Surely, there's some Gangrel Dragon coteries with Wyrm - but if you invest into being able to control your frenzies, then just having 1 dot merit and having the claws be agg at all times is probably better for you anyway, sooo.<br /> <br /> Enticing, Cutthroat, Atrocious - will give you 8 again, its not mindblowing. A point of WP spent, will probably give you better results than 8-again, unless you got extreme dice pools, but whatever. This is once per chapter ability. If anything, the drawbacks on enticing/cuttroat/atrocious, sound more thematic, and there to not have to deal with questions like &quot;What happens if I lose 10 again and gain 8 again simultaneously for something.&quot; or &quot;What if I lose 10 again twice, and shouldn't this be penalised further.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ye, it's possible that someone will find a merit where this would become an issue. It happens. The ruleslawyery min-max people are out there, who scour all the rules for loopholes, exist, it's up to the ST to go &quot;makes sense, I can see how RAW that's a loophole. But for the sake of <i>our tables </i>balance and fun I'm gonna say no.&quot; Or they might not, in which case that's a different table...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 06-17-2024, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T14:06:49-07:00","id":1537584,"title":"","content":"I think that covers everything and anyone including it in their game will probably have gotten it from here so hopefully their ST has read everything and can make their decision on everything raised.<br /> It\u2019s stood up to everything I can throw at it that said I would probably only use it as a free merit but it seems well priced for what it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T15:51:06-07:00","id":1537587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1536805-homebrew-oath-of-loyalty-a-coterie-connecting-oath?p=1537584#post1537584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that covers everything and anyone including it in their game will probably have gotten it from here so hopefully their ST has read everything and can make their decision on everything raised.<br /> It\u2019s stood up to everything I can throw at it that said I would probably only use it as a free merit but it seems well priced for what it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I do intend to give it out for free in my group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}